{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/489683-gangrel-bloodline-the-cerbat-hunt","id":489683,"title":"Gangrel Bloodline: The Cerbat Hunt","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-23T11:32:31-07:00","id":489683,"title":"Gangrel Bloodline: The Cerbat Hunt","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">At the moment, this is mostly Discipline rather than bloodline detailing itself; I've got a bare-bones narrative, but not much in the way of history besides that the founder of the bloodline ate her father in an attempt to drink down his knowledge of firearms, and was transfigured by his blood sorcery, an art for teaching the Beast how to act human; the two elements mixed and let her unleash the Beast through her father's gun by teaching the Beast how to fight like a human.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline</b>: The Cerbat Hunt<br /> <b>Bloodline Weakness</b>: <i>The Even-Handed Curse</i>. The Cannary suffer from the Gangrel clan weakness; the children of dust devils and the masters of the Man\u2019s murderous urge aren\u2019t exactly given to calmly and rationally working out their differences.<br /> <br /> In addition, the bloodline suffers another Curse; the assassin who lost his blood sorcery and his heartsblood to the line\u2019s founder, his daughter and someone else\u2019s childe, vowed on his rifle that the monster who ate his soul, and all that monster\u2019s damned descendants, would forever lose their charnel invincibility, their unfair advantage in every gunfight, and the curse caught and bubbled within his daughter's decrepit, murderous heart. Gunsels take lethal damage from firearms, like mortals: bullets tear through flesh jaggedly, as if they were magical, rather than lodging in useless organs, and they <i>burn </i>- it\u2019s a surprising amount of pain for any new inductee who\u2019s learned to think of a gun in prey\u2019s hands as an inconvenience rather than a murder weapon.<br /> <b>Disciplines</b>: Resilience, Animalism, Protean, <i>Gunnery</i><br /> <br /> <i><b>Gunnery</b></i><br /> <b>The Modern Death</b> (<i>\u2022</i>): The Gunsel can \u201cdevote\u201d a firearm so that it deals lethal damage to Kindred.<br /> <b>Cost</b>: (Size) Vitae + 1 Willpower<br /> <b>Requirement</b>: The vampire must anoint a firearm of Size 4 or less with her Vitae, which permanently marks it; encrusted blood seeps into the weapon or burns away once the Discipline is complete.<br /> <b>Dice Pool</b>: None<br /> <b>Action</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Indefinite<br /> <br /> In the All Night Society, a gun - the favorite negotiation tool of murderers since time damn well near immemorial - pales before something as atavistic, as savagely stupid, as <i>claws</i>. Not so for the Gunsel. By infusing her firearm with her Vitae, she can propel bullets not with something as weak as powder, but with the rage of the Beast that\u2019s learned how to fight like the Man.<br /> <br /> <b>Effect</b>: The Gunsel drips an amount of Vitae on the metal of her firearm equal to its Size to activate the Discipline. As the blood sinks in, iron and steel become stained, flecked with red spots; subtly, the curve of the barrel twists, and the trigger curls, until the firearm just slightly resembles the animal of the Gunsel\u2019s Beast - with a barrel that almost looks toothed, a scaled grip, shark-like sights, or what-have-you - as if it had been built by a smith inspired by the Gunsel\u2019s externalized Beast. This process takes about 5 minutes x the gun\u2019s Size.<br /> <br /> Bullets fired from a devoted firearm deal lethal damage to Kindred, inflicting the same feeling (of white-hot light jammed into a little hard ball) as all bullets that strike Gunsels, and are counted as magical weapons; devoted firearms are also more effective for their creators, gaining 9-again on all Firearms rolls. For other people, a devoted firearm locks up, and will not fire unless it is paid in life. Anyone can pay an amount of Vitae equal to the firearm's size or physically bleed on it (for an equivalent amount of lethal damage) to key it to themselves for one scene, allowing them to use it. If this has occurred, the Gunsel can key her devoted firearms back to herself with a touch and a turn of concentration. A Gunsel can devote a number of firearms equal to her Blood Potency at any given time.<br /> <br /> <b>Hematic Caliber</b> (<i>\u2022\u2022</i>): The Gunsel can load a firearm with \u201cblood bullets,\u201d sublimated from Vitae.<br /> <b>Cost</b>: 1 Vitae per clip<br /> <b>Requirement</b>: The vampire must drip Vitae into the ammunition chambers of the gun, unless she is loading a devoted firearm.<br /> <b>Dice Pool</b>: None<br /> <b>Action</b>: Instant or Reflexive<br /> <br /> Ordinary blood has a little iron content; Vitae is blood <i>par excellence</i>. With this Discipline, the Gunsel can sublimate iron-hard clots from her blood to fit a weapon.<br /> <br /> <b>Effect</b>: If the Gunsel is using a normal firearm, she must reload the weapon as normal, with the difference being that she leaks her own blood in lieu of actual ammunition; if she uses a devoted firearm, the blood immediately coalesces inside the chamber, without the need for its user to load it physically. One Vitae, for a normal gun, produces a full clip of characteristically reddish bullets, composed of hardened, inert blood. (For nonstandard ammunition sizes, more Vitae may be required.)<br /> <br /> Blood bullets, if removed from the chamber rather than fired, immediately begin to decay into flakes of dried blood, becoming unusable. This process also occurs once they\u2019ve struck a victim or come to a complete halt, making blood bullets generally superior to the standard for those looking not to be detected; however, Kindred Senses do apply to locating flakes of dried blood from a hemoglobin bullet.<br /> <br /> <b>Blood Will Out</b> (<i>\u2022\u2022\u2022</i>): The Gunsel\u2019s Kindred Senses function much more effectively against anyone with a bullet she fired embedded in them.<br /> <b>Cost</b>: None<br /> <b>Requirement</b>: The target must have been shot by the vampire, and have an untreated lethal wound caused by said.<br /> <b>Dice Pool</b>: None<br /> <b>Action</b>: None<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Blood Potency in nights<br /> <br /> <b>Effect</b>: Logically, if a gun is the extension of its owner, then so too are the bullets it fires. With this Discipline, the Gunsel can practically feel the flesh she shoots, and attune her senses to victims who haven\u2019t quite been finished off. She multiplies the range for her Kindred Senses by five against people with untreated gunshot wounds, and is treated as having tasted the blood of those she\u2019s shot for the purposes of tracking. If used against Kindred, with a devoted firearm (so the bullets will really <i>penetrate</i>), this Discipline may be invoked to increase the Gunsel\u2019s blood sympathy with the target by one step, to a maximum of Once-Removed, for her Blood Potency in nights.<br /> <br /> <i>Example</i>: Jane of the Unknown, a Gunsel with Blood Will Out, shoots Alan, a hunter, with her devoted pistol; she deals 3 lethal damage, but is briefly occupied by having to fend off and kill Alan\u2019s friends while he escapes. Normally, since she has Blood Potency 4, she can only hear heartbeats at twelve meters; luckily, Alan hasn\u2019t had time to dig out the bullet in his arm. Jane\u2019s range for hearing Alan\u2019s heartbeat increases to 60 meters, and she can smell his blood from 200 meters; since she\u2019s \u201ctasted\u201d it with her bullet, she can add her Blood Potency to rolls to track him by scent. Alan, sure that he\u2019s evaded her, sits down and starts trying to dig out the bullet with a knife, unaware of the bounty hunter coming ever closer\u2026<br /> <br /> <b>Kiss of Cordite</b> (<i>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</i>): The Gunsel can drain Vitae from bullet wounds at a distance.<br /> <b>Cost</b>: 1 Willpower<br /> <b>Requirement</b>: The target must have been shot by the vampire, and have an untreated lethal wound caused by said.<br /> <b>Dice Pool</b>: Manipulation + Firearms + Gunnery vs. Stamina + Supernatural Tolerance<br /> <b>Action</b>: Instant<br /> <br /> If the vampire\u2019s bullets are her teeth, then her throat can\u2019t be too far away. With this level of mastery of Gunnery, the Gunsel is able to reach out through the fear and the smell of smoke and drag little droplets of Vitae, sublimated to gas, through the air, until all her sight lines are hungry throats.<br /> <br /> <b>Effect</b>: To use this Discipline, the vampire\u2019s target must be within three times her Blood Potency in meters.<br /> <br /> <b>Dramatic Failure</b>: The vampire\u2019s attempt to feed only triggers the blood to heal her target\u2019s wounds. All lethal wounds on her target caused by her firearms attacks within the scene convert to bashing, and become inert for the purposes of Kiss of Cordite.<br /> <b>Failure</b>: The blood trickles, just for a second, but spills to the ground and becomes inert. The Gunsel cannot use Kiss of Cordite again until she inflicts more lethal wounds on her target.<br /> <b>Success</b>: The Gunsel drinks deeply through her leaden teeth. She gains an amount of Vitae equal to the lethal damage dealt by the relevant attack, instantly; this also inflicts the Scarred Condition, as if the Gunsel had fed violently on her target (since, essentially, she <i>has</i>).<br /> <b>Exceptional Success</b>: The Gunsel drains an extra lethal wound\u2019s worth of Vitae, dealing one lethal damage to the target.<br /> <br /> <b>Six-Chambered Beast</b> (<i>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</i>): The Gunsel, while frenzied or riding the wave, wields devoted firearms as extensions of herself.<br /> <b>Cost</b>: -<br /> <b>Requirement</b>: The vampire must be carrying a devoted firearm.<br /> <b>Dice Pool</b>: -<br /> <b>Action</b>: -<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Frenzy<br /> <br /> A devoted firearm is the power of the Beast, conducted through the medium of the Man - in the hands of the Beast, itself, it becomes an iron talon, an atavistic coil of stored thunder that kills unflinchingly, a culmination of firearm devotion.<br /> <br /> <b>Effect</b>: This Discipline triggers whenever the Gunsel enters anger or hunger frenzy, either involuntarily or through riding the wave, unless she throws her devoted gun away before entering frenzy.<br /> <br /> During frenzy:<ul><li>The vampire uses Gunnery Disciplines instinctively, and does not expend Vitae or Willpower to do so - feeding with Kiss of Cordite in hunger frenzy, or hunting down the injured with Blood Will Out - as long as she uses a devoted firearm.</li> <li>The Beast knows everything about its devoted firearms that the vampire knows, and uses that knowledge instinctively. It can, for example, assemble a devoted ceramic pistol or piece together a devoted shotgun that\u2019s been taken apart, take cover, aim before firing, refrain from wildly firing when using a devoted sniper rifle, etc.; while it is inclined to do whatever is expedient, if the Beast is trying to kill a rapidly fleeing target, it won\u2019t attempt to pursue on foot if it has access to a devoted gun that can hit from a distance. It won\u2019t use non-devoted guns, though - those are just lumps of strangely-shaped metal, not natural weapons.</li> <li>The vampire can temporarily convert firearms to devoted weapons. She reflexively spits 1 Vitae on a firearm, which immediately sinks in and violently deforms it in a second; weapons altered in this way do not count towards the vampire\u2019s maximum number of devoted firearms. Guns altered in this way lose all Structure and fall apart at the end of the scene, losing their devoted status.</li> <li>The vampire gains 8-again on Firearms rolls, and can spend 3 Vitae and 1 Willpower to make such a roll a rote action. The flow of blood and force through the devoted firearm necessary to accomplish this is hard on it; a normal devoted firearm suffers 1 Structure damage and becomes unusable until repaired, while temporary devoted firearms created through Six-Chambered Beast lose all Structure and burst, sloughing apart, without the capacity to contain the Beast flowing within; they become permanently unusable.</li> </ul><i><b>Devotions</b></i>:<br /> <b>Depraved Holster </b>(<i>Protean 2, Gunnery 1</i>)<br /> <b>Cost</b>: None; supplements Unmarked Grave and Predatory Aspect<br /> <b>Requirement</b>: The firearm involved must have been made devoted.<br /> <b>Dice Pool</b>: -<br /> <b>Action</b>: None<br /> <br /> <b>Effect</b>: When the Gunsel slumbers in her Unmarked Grave, the devoted firearms on her person, made mutable by the dreamlike sleep of earth and the thinning of Protean boundaries, can return to the Beast\u2019s own sheaf of weapons. When changing her adaptations in her Unmarked Grave, the Gunsel can consume one of her devoted firearms - as long as it\u2019s on her person - and gain the following adaptation as one of her three:<br /> <br /> <b>Tongue of Fire</b>: The Gangrel may extrude a gun from her flesh. She reflexively draws a devoted firearm, which she earlier consumed, from a rent in her flesh, or lets it bubble out of her veins and patch itself together; adaptations to her senses and hands give her 8-again with this firearm, and she cannot drop it, since it\u2019s fused to her hands in firing position, unless she chooses to let go. This also allows her to empower the gun with her Beast: every point of Vitae she spends increases the gun\u2019s Damage by 1 for one shot.<br /> <br /> The adaptation created by <i>Depraved Holster</i> is added to, and replaces, one of the three adaptations she has available. If she changes her adaptations in her Unmarked Grave, she may remove the Depraved Holster adaptation, but in the process, the Beast fully consumes and digests the weapon - so it\u2019s unwise to use this Devotion on your Touchstone heirloom flintlock.<br /> <br /> This Devotion costs 1 Experience. A variant of this Devotion exists, using <i>Protean 4</i> instead of <i>2</i> and with a cost of 3 Experiences:<br /> <b>Black Mamba</b> (<i>Protean</i> 4, <i>Gunnery</i> 2)<br /> <b>Cost</b>: None; supplements Unmarked Grave and Unnatural Aspect<br /> <b>Requirement</b>: The firearm involved must have been made devoted.<br /> <b>Dice Pool</b>: -<br /> <b>Action</b>: None<br /> <br /> <b>Effect</b>: Same as <i>Depraved Holster</i>, but the adaptation created is the following, replacing her Unnatural Aspect adaptation rather than one of her Predatory Aspect adaptations:<br /> <br /> <b>Black Mamba</b>: The gun and the Beast are one, and the Beast and the flesh are one. The Gunsel grows a mobile protuberance underneath her skin, interlaced with the mechanisms of an unpleasantly organic gun and attached to eyes designed to swiftly evaluate threats. The Gunsel can focus to extend the barrel and vision mechanism from any part of her body as a reflexive action, and may fire as an instant action, without using her hands or any part of her body; she takes no penalty for firing at things she can\u2019t see, thanks to the Mamba\u2019s eyes. She may also reload with <i>Hematic Caliber </i>at the same time that she aims.<br /> <br /> Relevant to this: I'm thinking of rewriting this to follow 2e's &quot;Bloodline Gift and Devotions&quot; format, rather than the current format. Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5757-calvaryketer","user":"CalvaryKeter","date":". 04-23-2015, 02:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5757-calvaryketer","name":"CalvaryKeter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5757_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}